# openbook.gfx.request: the graphics-mode request that OpenBook Graphics sets and init hands to openbook-gfx-mode
# (ANAL-246). init accepts a property trigger in a vendor .rc file only on a property vendor_init can read, so the
# platform side defines it on both tracks: a restricted platform property, readable by vendor_init. The same type and
# grant as gfx-mode/ruby/app-sepolicy.cil, which the Googlebook image's composer appends with the app's own domain.
# Without it the AOSP product logged a vendor_init read of default_prop at every boot (ANAL-319, QEMU).
system_restricted_prop(openbook_gfx_request_prop)
get_prop(vendor_init, openbook_gfx_request_prop)
